;; The Lonely Rover's opening (issue #61): the storm has weakened a section of the crater's rim
;; (racket/maps/victoria.rkt), and the world begins with it coming down, on screen, onto the
;; cargo that stands at its foot. Five crates up the slope from the cliff, along its middle
;; (azimuth 30); which the rubble buries, and under how much, is where the ground's physics
;; puts it, the same each run. The rim is rocky: 2% of what comes down comes down as 2 m
;; cubes of granite, 21.6 t each, which roll down the rubble and stop on it. Where the cargo
;; stands is the scenario's choice (#60). The battery bank's place was picked for its cover (owner
;; ruling 2026-10-09: about 1 m, not the 4 m it had at (264, 143)): the rubble thins down the slope
;; at about 0.39 m per metre (measured along the line from the cliff, crates 1 m apart: 3.99 m at
;; x = 262, 2.03 at 257, 1.24 at 255, 0.83 at 254), so (254.5, 137.9) is under 1.04 m. No boulder rests on the
;; bank (the nearest, boulder 5, lies 7.7 m away): the boulders stop on the thick rubble, and the thick rubble is
;; not here. Freeing the bank is optional (a vault can be built round it where it lies). A boulder is meant to
;; rest on a crate the win does not need, so that undermining it and levering it stay reachable (owner ruling
;; 2026-10-09): the solar-panels crate, moved from (254.62, 147.0) to (265.75, 143.5), lies under 2.15 m of
;; rubble (it was under 2.17 m) 1.78 m from boulder 4's centre (265.75, 141.72), a 21.6 t cube too big for a
;; backhoe to lift. The boulders do not move for a crate's place (measured: the same to 1 cm with the crate
;; anywhere), so the crate was put where the boulder lies; the two crates beyond the rubble's foot are bare, and
;; one of them holds the salvaged motors (found-motor): the generator is found, not built.
(world lonely-rover-opening
  ;; the scenario (#60): what this world is for, as the front end lists it. Every number is the real one but the bank's size: the found
  ;; 5 kWh bank at 0.1, 500 Wh, 5.6 h of a 90 W windmill (owner, 2026-10-09).
  (scenario
    (title "The Lonely Rover")
    (description "Mars, a crater, a storm that has brought a weakened rim down on your cargo. Find the battery bank under about a metre of rubble (dig it out, or build a vault round it where it lies), make electricity without panels, keep the bank warm through the night, and call Earth on the pre-dawn relay pass. The real numbers, with a 500 Wh bank.")
    (tuning (bank-capacity 0.1)))
  (map victoria)
  ;; the player's rover (#94): 45 m down the slope from the first crate, facing it (+x), where the floor is only ~7 degrees
  (rover (at 190.0 140.0) (heading 270))
  (place battery-bank found-bank (at 254.5 0 137.9))
  (place solar-panels cargo-crate (at 265.75 0 143.5))
  (place gas-cylinders cargo-crate (at 249.42 0 144.0))
  (place hand-tools cargo-crate (at 242.49 0 140.0))
  (place motors found-motor (at 233.83 0 135.0)))
